[1m[38;5;231mWhich tooling should be set up from the start?[0m

  [38;5;246m1.[39m [ ] Linting + formatting
  [38;5;246mESLint + Prettier on the stack's standard config, enforced from the first commit. Cheapest now, annoying to retrofit [39m
  [38;5;246macross a grown codebase.[39m
[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m2.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m [38;5;153mUnit test infrastructure[39m
  [38;5;246mA runner, a test layout, and one passing fixture. Needed for the log-fold invariant described above.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] End-to-end tests
  [38;5;246mBrowser-driven tests of the real page. Higher setup cost; catches the wiring that unit tests miss.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] Neither, keep it bare
  [38;5;246mPlain HTML/JS, no build step, no tooling. Fastest start, and each of the above gets harder to add later.[39m
